      "text": "```python\nimport os\nimport stat\n\n\ndef create_executable_file(path: str, data: bytes) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Create a binary file at path containing data and make it executable.\"\"\"\n    fd = os.open(path, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_TRUNC, 0o755)\n    with os.fdopen(fd, \"wb\") as f:\n        f.write(data)\n        f.flush()\n        os.fsync(f.fileno())\n\n    # O_TRUNC keeps the permissions of a pre-existing file, and the umask\n    # can strip bits on creation, so set the execute bits explicitly. Each\n    # execute bit is added only for classes that already have read permission.\n    mode = stat.S_IMODE(os.stat(path).st_mode)\n    readable_to_exec = (mode & (stat.S_IRUSR | stat.S_IRGRP | stat.S_IROTH)) >> 2\n    os.chmod(path, mode | readable_to_exec | stat.S_IXUSR)\n```",
